6. Attendance Module
This is the core feature of the application.

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.1 Daily Attendance State Machine
─────────────────────────────────────────

Each staff member follows a strict daily state transition:

  NOT_CHECKED_IN
       │
       ▼ (staff taps Check In + all validations pass)
  CHECKED_IN
       │
       ▼ (staff taps Check Out + all validations pass)
  CHECKED_OUT (final state for the day)

State Rules:
- NOT_CHECKED_IN  → Show "Check In" primary action button
- CHECKED_IN      → Show live elapsed shift timer + "Check Out" button
- CHECKED_OUT     → Show "Attendance Completed Today" badge (no further actions)
- Status resets to NOT_CHECKED_IN every day at midnight

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.2 Pre-Flight Diagnostics (Before Any Action)
─────────────────────────────────────────

Before Check-In or Check-Out is allowed, the app performs 4 mandatory checks:

  CHECK 1: Internet Connectivity
  - Uses @react-native-community/netinfo
  - If unavailable → Block attendance, show error

  CHECK 2: GPS / Location Services Enabled
  - Checks if device location is turned ON (system-level)
  - If disabled → Show "Enable GPS" action with deep link to device settings

  CHECK 3: Camera Permission
  - Checks CAMERA permission status
  - If denied → Show "Open App Settings" button for manual grant

  CHECK 4: Location Permission
  - Checks ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION (Android) / NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription (iOS)
  - If denied → Request permission, show rationale dialog

All 4 checks must pass before proceeding.

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.3 GPS Location Fetching
─────────────────────────────────────────

Once pre-flight checks pass, a fresh GPS fix is obtained:

  Config:
  - enableHighAccuracy: true
  - timeout: 15000ms (15 seconds)
  - maximumAge: 30000ms (reject cached fixes older than 30 seconds)
  - Accuracy threshold: Fixes with accuracy > 50 meters are rejected

  Output:
  - latitude (decimal degrees)
  - longitude (decimal degrees)
  - accuracy (meters)
  - timestamp (Unix epoch ms)
  - isMockLocation: boolean

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.4 Anti-Spoofing & Fake GPS Detection
─────────────────────────────────────────

Before geofence validation, the system checks for GPS spoofing:

  Android:
  - Reads Location.isFromMockProvider flag
  - Checks if developer options "Allow Mock Locations" is active

  iOS:
  - Detects isSimulatedLocation flag
  - Flags locations from known simulator coordinates

  If mock location is detected:
  - Attendance is HARD BLOCKED
  - User sees "Fake GPS Detected" error screen
  - Event is logged server-side for admin audit

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.5 Geofence Validation
─────────────────────────────────────────

After fetching a valid GPS fix, the distance to the school campus center is
calculated using the Haversine Geodesic Formula:

  distance = 2 × R × arcsin(√(sin²(Δφ/2) + cos(φ1)·cos(φ2)·sin²(Δλ/2)))

  where:
  - φ = latitude in radians
  - λ = longitude in radians
  - R = 6371000 meters (Earth radius)

  School anchor coordinates (Lat, Lon) are fetched dynamically from backend
  API on each session start and cached locally for 24 hours.

  Validation Logic:
  - distance <= schoolRadius (e.g. 150 meters) → INSIDE GEOFENCE (allow)
  - distance > schoolRadius → OUTSIDE GEOFENCE (block with distance message)

  The UI shows real-time live distance and a visual green/red indicator.

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.6 Check-In Full Flow
─────────────────────────────────────────

Step 1  User taps "Check In" on Dashboard or Attendance Home

Step 2  Pre-Flight Diagnostics run
        Internet ✓ | GPS ✓ | Camera ✓ | Location Permission ✓

Step 3  Fresh GPS coordinates fetched
        (accuracy < 50m, age < 30s, not mock)

Step 4  Fake GPS check performed
        Blocked if mock location detected

Step 5  Haversine distance calculated
        Employee must be within school geofence radius

Step 6  Front Camera opens automatically
        Gallery selection is disabled
        Face alignment oval overlay is shown

Step 7  Employee captures a Live Selfie
        Photo is displayed in preview screen with:
        - Location watermark (School Name, Lat, Lon)
        - Date & Time overlay
        - Employee Name & ID overlay

Step 8  Employee taps "Confirm Check In"

Step 9  App submits multipart payload to server:
        - Employee ID
        - Attendance Type: check_in
        - Latitude
        - Longitude
        - GPS Accuracy
        - Device Timestamp
        - Device ID / UUID
        - App Version
        - Selfie Image (JPEG compressed)

Step 10 Server validates payload and returns confirmation

Step 11 Daily state transitions to CHECKED_IN
        Success screen shown with check-in timestamp
        Late flag shown if check-in time exceeds grace period

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.7 Check-Out Full Flow
─────────────────────────────────────────

Identical to Check-In flow with following differences:
- Attendance Type: check_out
- State transitions from CHECKED_IN → CHECKED_OUT
- Success screen shows: Check-In Time | Check-Out Time | Total Working Hours
- Early check-out flag is applied if check-out is before shift end time

─────────────────────────────────────────
6.8 Late / Early Flags
─────────────────────────────────────────

  Late Check-In:
  - Flag applied if check-in time > school start time + grace period
  - Example: If school starts at 9:00 AM and grace period is 15 minutes,
    any check-in after 9:15 AM is marked LATE

  Early Check-Out:
  - Flag applied if check-out time < minimum shift end time
  - Example: If minimum shift is 6 hours, leaving before minimum hours is flagged

  These flags are stored server-side and visible in Attendance History.

7. Attendance Validation Rules
Attendance will be accepted only when:
Internet is Available
GPS is Enabled (system-level)
GPS accuracy is <= 50 meters
GPS fix is not older than 30 seconds
Mock / Fake GPS is NOT detected
Camera Permission is Granted
Location Permission is Granted
Employee is inside School Geofence Radius
Live Selfie is Captured (gallery upload blocked)
Daily state allows the action (not already checked out)
Serverside timestamp validation passes
Otherwise attendance will be rejected with a specific user-friendly error message.

Error Scenarios & Messages:
  OUTSIDE_GEOFENCE      → "You are X meters away from school. Please be within Y meters."
  MOCK_GPS_DETECTED     → "Fake GPS detected. Attendance cannot be marked."
  NO_INTERNET           → "No internet connection. Please connect and try again."
  GPS_DISABLED          → "GPS is disabled. Please enable location services."
  LOW_ACCURACY          → "GPS accuracy is too low. Move to an open area and retry."
  CAMERA_DENIED         → "Camera access required. Please grant permission in settings."
  ALREADY_CHECKED_IN    → "You have already checked in today."
  ALREADY_CHECKED_OUT   → "You have already completed attendance for today."
  SERVER_ERROR          → "Server error. Please try again in a moment."

